ized), leaving the criterion's key clause under-specified as an in-session measurable outcome.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f41fdffa571f9d3d0","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"n394365e27961e893","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression that silently falls back to full materialization would still pass a byte-parity check while violating the stated performance intent."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an assertion on the object-read count or read set captured by the receipt (bounded to the requested subset) to the parity test named in step 7.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["8 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a retry bound (or backoff + surface-error termination) for the push-rejection revalidate/retry loop so a repeatedly-losing pusher fails visibly rather than looping.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'On rejection, fetch and revalidate: rebuild/retry an unrelated delta or restart verification for a relevant delta'","No maximum-retry count, backoff strategy, or give-up/surface-error condition is stated for repeated fast-forward rejections."],"finding":"The push-rejection path says 'fetch and revalidate: rebuild/retry an unrelated delta or restart verification for a relevant delta' but states no retry bound, backoff, or termination condition, so a repeatedly-losing pusher could loop indefinitely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb6d4c04b736a1840","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 6 / Rollout","norm_id":"n5e41e063d945d1ea","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A busy tracker where many concurrent normal writes keep advancing HEAD, causing a close run to repeatedly rebuild and re-lose the push race."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a bounded retry policy (e.g. N attempts with backoff, then surface a close-failed error preserving prior HEAD) to step 6 and add a metric for retry count.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define a RETIRE/eviction path (TTL, LRU, or prune-on-startup by liveness) for OID-keyed derived resolver/graph indexes so stale-OID entries do not accumulate unbounded.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7025,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Put derived resolver/graph indexes outside the immutable tree and key them by tracker OID plus schema version.'","'Derived caches are OID/schema-keyed with per-run temporaries and do not write inside the pinned view.'","ABSENCE: no eviction, TTL, or cleanup path named for OID-keyed cache entries whose tracker OID is no longer live."],"finding":"The plan defines derived resolver/graph indexes keyed by tracker OID plus schema version, but specifies no RETIRE/eviction path for stale OID-keyed cache entries. Because these caches are keyed by tracker OID, every normal write advances the tracker and produces a new cache key, so entries for superseded OIDs accumulate without bound.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc558edfc8d202ea6","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 / AC 'Derived caches are OID/schema-keyed with per-run temporaries'","norm_id":"n7510e213f3f17386","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Long-running dogfood: after thousands of normal writes advance the tracker, the derived-index store accumulates one keyed entry per historical OID and grows unbounded on disk."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a bounded cache policy: cap the derived-index store by count/size with LRU eviction, or prune entries whose tracker OID is no longer reachable from live refs.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify cleanup/reclamation of per-run temporary paths on abort, restart, or crash (not only on the in-lock commit rollback).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7025,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'prepare the verdict, receipt digest, completion certificate payload, event UUIDs, and all work not requiring final HLC order. Each run owns ... unique temporary paths.'","'Any signing, staging, index, or commit fault rolls back only this bundle and restores pre-operation state.'","ABSENCE: no cleanup path named for the unique temporary paths when the run aborts outside the commit rollback window."],"finding":"Per-run temporary paths are prepared outside the write lock (step 4), but the plan specifies rollback of the committed-store bundle only for the in-lock commit (step 5). It does not state who cleans up per-run temporaries when preparation succeeds but the run aborts before or during the lock (e.g. push-rejection restart, HEAD-assertion failure, or a crash between step 4 and step 5).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a91e4840cbb1589","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 4 (out-of-lock preparation) and step 5 (in-lock rollback)","norm_id":"n86fe2c0d6a7f1c9c","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A run prepares temporaries, then push is rejected and verification restarts at Tn (step 6), leaving orphaned temporary paths from the prior attempt.","Process crash between preparation and commit leaves per-run temporary paths with no reclamation."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm that the atomic-publication boundary genuinely depends on the pinned-read basis (receipt validation at Tn); if the two halves are separable, consider splitting into a read-path child and a write-path child.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["G5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4167,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Title: 'Use a lazy pinned ticket view and atomically publish completion-close artifacts'.","Context motivates two distinct problems: 'materializes the full Git-backed ticket store' (perf) AND 'A durable PASS can outlive a failed close' (atomicity).","Coupling: step 3 validates the pinned receipt before the atomic write; step 5 asserts HEAD==validated Tn."],"finding":"The title joins two goals with 'and' — a lazy pinned ticket view (read-path optimization) and atomic close-artifact publication (write-path correctness fix). Each half is independently valuable and separately testable: the lazy view addresses the 135-235s materialization cost; the atomic bundle addresses durable-PASS-outliving-failed-close. They are coupled only through the receipt-as-stable-read-basis; the plan should confirm this coupling is load-bearing enough to keep them one unit rather than two children.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f31d4ff61aff82540","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Title and Context ('one stable read basis and one atomic publication boundary')","norm_id":"n1ca96d2b4b89581b","priority":0.1833,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The lazy view could ship and deliver the perf w